From 1e93ae8ddced320299828d59791cba2e95171ae3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:27:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 020/118] rule-set: bound a remote fetch by stalls, start
 without a list that does not come

A remote rule-set was fetched with no deadline: a download that stalled
at start held the start, and with it DNS for the LAN, until TCP gave up
(about 16 minutes).

- Every fetch is cancelled once no data has come for 30 s; a slow but
  steady download goes on for as long as it progresses.
- At start the fetch has 30 s in all: then the set starts empty (the
  existing failed-start path) and the updater loads it in the
  background. A failed start fetch drops the pooled connections, so the
  next batch of sets does not wait on the same dead one.
- The error says which bound cut the fetch.
- Bodies over 50 MB are refused.
- 1.14: a set that started empty reports its content as unknown (mixed)
  until it is loaded, so the DNS router does not fix a mode that the
  arriving list would then be rejected under.
- The rules are read and dropped under the set's lock: since the start
  deadline they are routinely swapped while connections match them.
